      "dom_id": "question-9985",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the sum to infinity of the geometric series $0.8+0.2+0.05+0.012\\,5+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=0.8$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{0.2}{0.8}=0.25.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.8}{1-0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.8}{0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{75} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
