      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n-7.5+1.5-0.3+0.06+⋯.\n$$\n\n Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-7.5$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1.5}{-7.5}=-0.2.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7.5}{1-(-0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7.5}{1+0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7.5}{1.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-75}{12} \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
